---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import EnquiryForm from '../components/EnquiryForm.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { processFaqs } from '../data/faqs';

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: processFaqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<Layout
  title="How a worktop install works, from survey to fitting"
  description="What happens between your enquiry and your finished worktops: the template visit, fabrication, and install day. Realistic timescales and exactly what your kitchen needs to be ready."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h1>From enquiry to finished worktops.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Three visits at most: template, install, and a second template visit only if you are having
        full-height splashbacks. Here is what happens and what we need from you at each stage.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage__text prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">Step 1</span>
          <h2>Quote</h2>
          <p>
            Send us the kitchen plan, or a sketch with rough dimensions, through the
            <a href="/contact#enquire">enquiry form</a>. Tell us the material you are thinking about, or
            say you are not sure. We reply with an indicative price and the next available survey date,
            {site.leadTimes.enquiryToSurvey}.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you want to go ahead, we send a written quote and specification: material, colour,
            thickness, edge profile, cut-outs, upstands, and the price including VAT and fitting. You
            approve that in writing before anything is ordered.
          </p>
          <p class="notice notice--review">
            REVIEW: Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013. Because this is a made-to-measure contract
            agreed off-premises or at a distance, the pre-contract information (the specification, total
            price, delivery and install timescales, our complaints process, and the fact that the
            14-day cancellation right does not apply to goods made to the consumer's specification)
            must be given in a durable form before the customer is bound. That means before the deposit
            is taken. Check this wording and the quote template with an adviser.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Placeholder caption="A kitchen plan marked up for quoting" ratio="4 / 3" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage__text prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">Step 2</span>
          <h2>Template</h2>
          <p>
            One of our templaters visits and takes a digital template of the fitted units. This takes
            about an hour for a normal kitchen. We agree the position of joins and the exact cut-outs
            with you on the day, and confirm the specification.
          </p>
          <h3>Your kitchen needs to be ready. That means:</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>All base units fitted, fixed to the wall, and level.</li>
            <li>End panels, wall panels and appliance housings in place.</li>
            <li>The sink, hob and taps on site, in their boxes is fine. We template around the real thing, not a spec sheet.</li>
            <li>Any undermount sink fitted to its unit if the fitter is doing that.</li>
            <li>Old worktops removed, unless we have agreed to remove them.</li>
            <li>Range cookers and freestanding appliances in position.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If the kitchen is not ready when we arrive, we cannot template. We will need to rebook, and
            a wasted visit may be charged. We will phone the day before to check.
          </p>
          <p>
            If anything moves after the template, tell us before fabrication. Worktops are cut to the
            template. They will not fit units that have been moved.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Placeholder caption="Templating a fitted kitchen" ratio="4 / 3" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage__text prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">Step 3</span>
          <h2>Fabrication</h2>
          <p>
            The stone is cut, edged and polished to the template. This normally takes
            {site.leadTimes.templateToInstall}. Ultra-compact and some granites take longer, and we will
            tell you if yours will.
          </p>
          <p>
            We will confirm the install date once the pieces are ready. If you have a fitter or
            plumber waiting to come back, book them for after the install, not the same day.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Placeholder caption="Slab being cut on the saw" ratio="4 / 3" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="stage__text prose">
          <span class="eyebrow">Step 4</span>
          <h2>Install day</h2>
          <p>
            Two fitters arrive with the pieces. A typical kitchen takes half a day. A large kitchen
            with an island, waterfall ends or full-height splashbacks can take a full day.
          </p>
          <h3>What we do</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Dry-fit every piece and check it against the units.</li>
            <li>Fix down, join, and fill joins with colour-matched resin.</li>
            <li>Fit upstands and seal to the wall.</li>
            <li>Seal granite. Clean everything down.</li>
            <li>Walk you round it before we leave.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3>What we need</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Someone to let us in and be contactable during the day.</li>
            <li>Clear access from the van to the kitchen. Tell us about steps, narrow doors or upper floors when you enquire.</li>
            <li>Water and power.</li>
            <li>Units clear of anything you do not want dusty.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not plumb in sinks or connect hobs. Your plumber and electrician can do that the next
            day, once the resin has cured.
          </p>
          <h3>After</h3>
          <p>{site.guarantee.summary}. {site.guarantee.remedy}.</p>
        </div>
        <Placeholder caption="Fitters setting a worktop on install day" ratio="4 / 3" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <Faq items={processFaqs} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <EnquiryForm />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .stage {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .stage {
      grid-template-columns: 3fr 2fr;
    }
  }
</style>
